<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<speak version="1.0" xml:lang="en-GB">
  <!-- AI CUE: TITLE: clear and composed; give the heading room. Do not perform as narrative prose. -->
  <p><s>Chapter 68: Under the Arch</s></p><break time="700ms"/>
  <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He'd been under the beam since the morning of the hundred-and-fortieth day.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He'd lain on his belly on the rotten boards with his face to the crack in the wall, all that day and the night after and the day after that, and moved only to turn on his side when his hip went dead. When it rained in the night it came in through the broken top of the tower and ran down the inside of the wall, and he put his mouth to the stone and drank. He had nothing to eat. He didn't think about it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>Below him, in the round room at the foot of the tower, the two guards sat by the door. They changed at noon and dusk. They talked about home, about their feet, about the soup. One of them was from Cotter's Cross and missed his wife. The other was from somewhere on the coast and didn't miss anybody. Under them, in the floor, the stair went down to the slab with the iron plate in it, and nobody went down it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Very far off in the north, the three of them. He felt them all the time. Kharrak pacing. Lisska awake, worrying, round and round like a dog at a shut door. Aurveth lying still, but not asleep.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>Not yet, he thought at them. Stay.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The second man came at dusk on the hundred-and-forty-first day.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Calder heard him before he saw him. From the east. From across the channel, from the Eelweir, where the whole Saltreach bank was campfires now, up the hill behind Harrow's End and along both sides of the beck. A sound went up from there in the dusk. Men cheering. A lot of men, on and on, the way the crowd had cheered on the Tidesteps at Wendmouth when the man came out onto the top step and threw his arms wide.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Then boats. The knock of oars. Lanterns on the water.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He pressed his face to the crack.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He could see the slope down to the spit through the broken top of the eastern gate. A boat came in to the gravel in the last of the light with lanterns at bow and stern, and men jumped out into the shallows and held it, and a man stood up in the bow.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Tall. In grey, with no armour. Bareheaded. He stood in the bow of the boat in the lantern light with the water round its keel and looked up the slope at the fort, at the fires, at the men coming down from the gate to meet him, and laughed.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Calder heard it from the tower. That laugh. He'd heard it on the Tidesteps at noon with three thousand people round him.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>The man jumped down into the water to his knees, and came up the gravel, and the men on the slope crowded round him. He took their hands. He put his arm round one. He walked up the slope toward the fort in the middle of them, talking, laughing, touching shoulders, the way he'd walked down the Tidesteps among the crowd, and the men round him laughed when he laughed.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He came in through the eastern gate. Across the fort. Toward the tower. Toward the arch.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>The still man was waiting under the arch.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>He'd been there since noon. Standing under the verse with his hands behind his back. He stayed where he was when the other came across the fort toward him. He didn't go to meet him. He waited.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The laughing man came up to the arch and stopped. A pace off.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>They stood there. Under the verse. In the light of the great fire in the middle of the fort, a pace apart, facing each other.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Calder looked down at them through the crack in the wall.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The same face.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Long. Pale. Clean-shaven. Dark hair cut short. The same height, the same narrow shoulders, the same long hands. He looked from one to the other and back again and couldn't find a difference, in the face or in the bones.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The difference was in everything else. One stood with his hands behind his back and didn't move, not his head, not his hands, not his weight from one foot to the other. Like a stone. Like something carved. The other couldn't keep still. He shifted his weight. He put a hand up and pushed his hair back. He smiled.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>There's two of them, thought Calder.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>It went through him like cold water into his boots.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>There were always two of them.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>The Tidesteps, at noon, on the forty-ninth day. And the carter at the ford below Cotter's Cross on the sixty-first, with his story of Ferriby. The leader himself on the smithy roof, directing it. At dusk, on the forty-ninth. A hundred leagues. Then he's got wings, the carter had said, and Calder had thought of Aurveth, and not been able to make it add up.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He hadn't needed wings. He'd needed a brother.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Corvin," said the laughing one.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Cassian," said the still one.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>That was all, at first. They stood there and said each other's names, as you'd say the name of a man you saw every day. Then the laughing one, Cassian, put out his hand and gripped his brother's shoulder, once, and let go. Corvin let it happen.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"You've had a quiet day, brother," said Cassian.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I've had a long one." Corvin's voice was low and even. It didn't carry. Calder had to hold his breath to hear it, and the guards at the tower door below him had stopped talking. "The knights came up from Greyhold this morning. All of them. Two hundred and sixty riders, the hounds, the captain's pig in a cage. And the chain, on a wain." He tilted his head very slightly toward the west, toward the far bank, where Calder could see from his crack a long line of fires along the reeds below Redwatch. "Opposite. Facing the ladders."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Rowan too?"</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Rowan too. At the head of it."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>Cassian laughed. Softly, this time. "Bless her. She's done exactly what we wanted."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"She had no choice." Corvin didn't smile. "Fewer than forty on Greyhold's wall. The weapons master, the old archivist, some students, the old and the hurt." He paused. "Our friend is among them."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"And Millbrook?"</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Millbrook's ready. The barns are full, Reede says. Fennick's, the tithe barn, the boats on the back channel." Corvin looked at his brother. "They'll be waiting when you cross."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"And Halloran's woman?"</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Lent to Delling. Goes with you. For the gate." Corvin didn't look round. "She's worth a ram at a gate. Once."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Twice, she says."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Once and a half. Then she'll want carrying." Corvin was quiet a moment. "The Fellow stays here. With me."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Calder didn't know the word. Below the arch, a little way off by the fire, a small grey man in a long brown gown sat on a stone with his hands between his knees, and didn't look up at it.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Somebody was coming up from the spit.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Calder heard him on the gravel before he saw him. Then he came into the light of the fire, crossing the fort toward the arch. A man of no particular height. Brownish hair. Brownish beard. A face that went out of your head while you looked at it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>Rook stopped a little way off from the two of them, as a servant stops, and waited.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Well?" said Corvin.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"The boats are all over," said Rook. "The last of the cages. The smoke's at the pit, in case it comes back in the night. Delling's men are on the west shore with the ladders." His voice was pleasant and ordinary. "And there's word from the north. From the Clan."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Calder's hand closed on the hilt of Joss's knife.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"The old one of the ledges is dead," said Rook. "The one who went down the hill at the second ford. And his dragon after him. They carried them to Coldtarn." He paused. "And the Clan's still fighting. Arn's riders burned a Skarrow farm two nights ago. There was some paper. Some old woman of the ledges read it out in both yards." He almost laughed. "About me, I'm told. Nobody believed her."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Nobody?" said Corvin.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Arn threw her out of the hold. Ulric listened to the end and didn't say anything and went back in." Rook shrugged. "Either way, they're not coming south. Not this side of the summer."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Good," said Corvin.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Cassian had turned away a little. He was looking at the fire.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"The old man," he said. "On the dragon. At the ford."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"He came down," said Rook. "Nobody thought he would. The rest of them sat there under their law the way we said they would, long enough. He came down." He shrugged again. "Somebody put a bolt in him. It happens."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"It happened at the mill," said Cassian.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"That one didn't happen." Rook said it mildly, as you'd put a man right about the price of barley. "That one was bought. One of Delling's crossbows, in the hedge at the bottom of the field, before we'd hired the rest of the company. Paid to put the woman on the green one out of the fight if the other two came down. So the war-pairs would break, all three, in one night, and the dragons would be loose." He shrugged. "They broke. The dragons went to a farmer in a barley field. Nobody paid for that."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Thock. In the dark, by the hedge. Calder had heard it lying in the stubble with his ribs stove in, and not known what it was until it was too late to matter.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>Far off in the north something went quiet all at once, like birds in a hedge when a hawk's shadow crosses it. Lisska. He felt her go still. He felt Imra's cold come up through the green mark the way it had come on the night of the mill, and Teo's name in it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"It did what it was for," said Corvin. "The Clan won't stand together again this side of the summer. That's all we needed." He turned his head and looked at his brother. "You knew what the ford was for."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I knew." Cassian didn't turn round. "I didn't know about the old man."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Nobody ever knows about the old man," said Corvin. "There's always one."</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Calder lay on the boards with his face to the crack.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>He couldn't feel his hand on the knife. He'd been gripping it so hard the hand had gone dead. He knew he should let go. He didn't.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Below him, Cassian turned round from the fire.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"The boy," he said.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Rook looked at him.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"The first one." Cassian's voice had gone quiet. Not warm now. Careful. "At the first ford. In the autumn. Varr's son. The young one." He looked at Rook. "I've never asked."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"No," said Rook. "You haven't."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I'm asking."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Rook looked at Corvin. Corvin didn't move.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Tell him," said Corvin.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Rook shrugged.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I went down before light," he said. "From Ulric's camp. Took a horse. Said I was going to the coast for my mother. Nobody missed me; nobody ever does." He said it without any pride at all, as a man says what time he got up. "Rode it hard. Lay up in the gorse above the ford till he came. He came down alone at first light. Before his men. Before anybody. He always did, the steward said. He wanted to be first." He paused. "He was pleased to see me. Waved. He thought I'd come down from Ulric's people to be at the meeting. To hold the horses. He got down off his horse at the edge of the water and held the reins out to me."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>The fire cracked.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"He never drew," said Rook. "He went in the water like a stone."</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>The stair under Calder was very quiet. The guards at the tower door weren't moving. He could hear the fire in the fort and the river going past the island on both sides and his own heart.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He was pleased to see me.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He was in the beck to his knees, with Teo in his arms, and Teo's head going back over his arm, and his face the same face, long and thin and too young, with the eyes open and the mouth a little open as if he'd been about to say something cheerful.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He held the reins out to me.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Leave the armband?" said Corvin.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"On the alders. Plain grey, no thread, the way you said. And a Clan axe in the shallows." Rook nodded slightly. "The farmer found them. Arn found the farmer. It went the way you said it would."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Cassian turned away again. He stood with his back to them looking at the fire, with one hand pushed up into his hair, and stayed like that.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>Corvin watched him.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"You wanted the one realm," said Corvin quietly. "You made three thousand people weep for it at Wendmouth. This is what it costs." He didn't raise his voice. "Rook pays it. I pay it. You stand on the steps."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Cassian didn't answer.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I'd still rather have the farmer than burn him," he said at last, to the fire. "That's all. I'd rather have him. He's the sign. The man with three. Whatever the old books say, it's a beautiful thing, Corvin, a man three dragons lie down round in a field. It's the one realm in a single man. Think of him on the steps beside me. If we could only bring him in…"</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"We'll have the dragons either way," said Corvin. "A man's a halter. So's the girl. You don't need to love the halter."</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Corvin turned and looked up.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>Calder stopped breathing.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>But the eyes didn't come to the crack. They went to the verse. Over the arch, six lines, square and spare, in the firelight. Corvin looked at it the way he'd looked at it the day before: reading it. All of it. The parts that were there and the parts that were gone.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Then he looked down. At the threshold. At the long smooth hollow worn in the stone, where the lion had lain.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"She took it off the island in the dark," he said. "The night before we came. The knight-girl. Delling's men found the skiff-mark at the west shore and its prints going into the water beside hers." He was quiet a moment. "I'd have liked to have it here. At the hour. It came back to this door every night for three hundred years. It would have come back tomorrow."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"It might yet," said Cassian. "Give it the night."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"It might." Corvin turned his head and looked west, across the island, across the channel, toward the dark Hearthmere bank and the line of the knights' fires. "We don't need it. We need the hour, and two hands." He looked at his brother. "Tomorrow Millbrook rises and you knock on the gate, loud, so they look at it. Spend Halloran's woman on it, all she has. A knock that costs us nothing, the gate won't believe. The night after, our friend opens it and takes you down. Under the school. To the knight's lock."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"And you stay here."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I stay here." Corvin moved his foot. He tapped the floor of the arch with the toe of his boot, once, lightly. On the threshold, at the edge of the hollow. Toward the tower, toward the round room behind him where the stair went down to the slab and the iron plate. "With this one."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"At the hour."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"At the hour. Not before. Not after." Corvin's voice didn't change at all. "Midnight, the night after tomorrow. Never mind the moon. The same breath. Here, and there. If one turns and the other doesn't, nothing opens and they know we're there. Both, or nothing."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Two hands," said Cassian.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Two hands."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>Neither of them said what the locks opened. Neither of them said what was under the school or under the tower or under the river between. They stood under the arch a pace apart, the same face twice, and Calder lay above them and waited for one of them to say it, and neither did. Neither of them needed to, by the sound of it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>When two hands open what one hand shut.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>His mother at Bel's table, with her hands flat on the wood.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>It wakes, and it will not sleep again.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Cassian went back to the boat a little after.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>He went down the slope to the spit with men round him again, with the lanterns, and Calder watched him go through the broken top of the eastern gate, and he was laughing again by the time he reached the gravel. Taking hands. Putting his arm round shoulders. He got into the bow of the boat and stood up in it and lifted both arms, and from the Eelweir and the whole black hill behind Harrow's End the cheer went up again, on and on.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The boat didn't go back to the Eelweir. It went south. Downriver. Down the east channel and round the south end of the island and out into the main stream, toward the Hearthmere side, toward the bend below where Greyhold was, and Millbrook. Its lanterns went out one by one as it went, until there was nothing.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>Corvin stood under the arch and watched it go.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He stood there with his hands behind his back until the last lantern was gone. Then he went away across the fort toward the great fire in the middle, and the men there made way for him without being asked.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Rook didn't go.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He sat down on the step of the tower door. Below Calder. Right below him, with the guards on either side, at the foot of the wall Calder was lying against. He took a knife out of his belt. A knife with a round pommel. He took a bit of wood out of his pocket, and began to whittle.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Calder could hear the knife. Small. Steady. The shavings falling on the step.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>He lay under the beam and thought about it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>It would be easy. The broken stair came down round the inside of the wall to the door. In the dark. Twenty steps, maybe. Rook on the step at the bottom with his back to the tower, whittling, and two guards beside him half asleep. He'd be on him before the guards were up. Joss's knife. One blow.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>He'd never killed anybody with his own hand. He'd let Kharrak. He'd said yes on Aurveth's neck in the dark at the Ewe Beck and three men had died, and he'd thought about them every night since. He'd never done it himself.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He was pleased to see me. He held the reins out to me.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He took his hand off the knife. It wouldn't open at first. He had to make it, one finger at a time.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He lay there with his dead hand against his chest, over the rubbing under his shirt, and the chains.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He had it now. Not proof. You couldn't hold it up in a yard. You couldn't scrub it with ash and find two little hammers under the six. But he had it. The words. Out of their own mouths. He never drew. He went in the water like a stone. Leave the armband? On the alders. It did what it was for.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He'd heard it. Him. Lying under a beam in the dark with his face to a crack.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>It was worth exactly as much as everything else he'd carried all winter. A farmer's word. A man who'd been at both fords and found both bodies. The dragon farmer says he heard them. In the tower. In the dark. Nobody else.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He needed somebody to hear it who wasn't him.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He needed Rook alive.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Below him the knife went on, small and steady, on the step.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Far off in the north, the three of them, and Kharrak's temper going up hot. He'd felt it. Of course he had. He'd felt whatever had gone through Calder when Rook said like a stone, all the way to the hatching caves.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>Not yet, thought Calder. Stay. Not yet.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>He felt Kharrak not want to. He felt Aurveth's slow weight settle over it, the way she'd stood over him at the mouth of the cave.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>On the far bank, along the reeds below Redwatch, the knights' fires burned in a long line.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>On the island the fires burned everywhere.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>And under him, under the round room and the two guards and Rook whittling on the step, under the choked stair and the slab with the iron plate, under the island and the river and the whole of the night, so far down he wasn't sure if he felt it or heard it, something turned over in the dark and was still again.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>Two hands, he thought. Here, and under the school.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The night after tomorrow.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>He lay under the beam and didn't sleep, and listened to the knife.</p>
<break time="450ms"/></speak>
